    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65994" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελί̆-γηρυς</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελί̆-γᾱρυς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">υος</span>, ὁ, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sweet-voiced, melodious</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄψ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					12.187
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀοιδή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Ap.</u>
					519
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρθενικαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alcm.
					26.1
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕμνοι, κῶμοι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				11(10).4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>N.</u>
				3.4
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παιᾶνος ὀμφά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pae.</u>
					5.47
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀηδών</span>, of a woman, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				14.1942
			</span></i>.—Poet. word, used by <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				269a
			</span></i>.</div>
